WEBVTT

00:02.281 --> 00:03.658
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.741 --> 00:05.566
- Let me ask you something.
- Anything.

00:05.660 --> 00:07.484
How'd you know Claire was drowning?

00:20.925 --> 00:22.093
Claire!

00:23.511 --> 00:26.139
I could hear her calling for help.

00:26.431 --> 00:29.632
You hear the lightning as well?

00:44.323 --> 00:48.453
I wasn't saving Claire, Charlie.
I was saving you.

00:49.370 --> 00:54.667
When I saw the lightning hit the roof,
you were electrocuted.

00:54.751 --> 00:58.536
And when you heard Claire
was in the water, you...

00:58.629 --> 01:01.549
You drowned trying to save her.

01:01.632 --> 01:05.167
I've tried, brother,
I've tried twice to save you, but...

01:05.261 --> 01:06.804
No matter what I try to do...

01:09.432 --> 01:11.841
...you're gonna die, Charlie.

01:25.156 --> 01:26.491
You're insane, mate.

01:26.908 --> 01:31.402
Superman can fly around the
entire planet in the blink of an eye.

01:31.496 --> 01:34.415
Dude, if we're going by
a pure foot race,

01:34.499 --> 01:36.375
Supes would get dusted by the Flash.

01:36.459 --> 01:40.505
Why would the Man of Steel
agree to a sodding foot race?

01:40.797 --> 01:42.840
For charity.

01:42.924 --> 01:47.178
And Flash would totally win, because
he can vibrate through walls and stuff.

01:47.261 --> 01:51.808
Vibration! Whatever would Superman do
if he came up against a wall?

01:51.891 --> 01:53.799
Well, no smashing allowed.

01:54.352 --> 01:58.106
No flying, no smashing... Any other
restrictions I need to know about?

01:58.189 --> 02:01.192
Perhaps we should fit Superman
with a pair of kryptonite...

02:03.611 --> 02:04.643
What the hell?

02:10.159 --> 02:11.244
Charlie!

02:13.079 --> 02:15.039
- Don't touch it!
- Oh, my God. Oh, my God!

02:15.123 --> 02:16.207
Just breathe...

02:17.125 --> 02:19.335
Don't try to talk.
We've got to get him back.

02:19.419 --> 02:21.160
- No! You help!
- I can't help!

02:23.423 --> 02:24.799
I'm sorry, mate.

02:48.072 --> 02:50.366
<i>Superman can fly</i>
<i>around the entire planet.</i>

03:23.149 --> 03:26.183
Hey! Where's the wire?

03:27.403 --> 03:29.812
You eat those mushrooms
Jack warned us about?

03:29.906 --> 03:33.826
Listen to me. There's a wire,
a cable, buried in the sand.

03:35.369 --> 03:37.194
Do you know what I'm talking about?

03:37.955 --> 03:41.459
- This is future crap, isn't it?
- The cable! Do you know where it is?

03:43.086 --> 03:45.661
- This is important.
- Why?

03:48.174 --> 03:49.550
<i>Superman.</i>

03:55.306 --> 03:57.047
Because someone's coming.

04:50.755 --> 04:53.330
God tests our faith in many ways.

04:53.424 --> 04:57.261
As you well know,
we have our own test here.

04:57.345 --> 05:01.641
A vow of silence that lasts
as long as we see fit.

05:01.724 --> 05:07.730
This challenges both
one's patience and his faith.

05:07.939 --> 05:11.140
For some it may last a week,

05:11.234 --> 05:14.403
those we're less sure about, a month.

05:15.321 --> 05:17.646
Personally, Desmond,

05:17.740 --> 05:20.034
I never thought you'd last.

05:22.286 --> 05:24.497
And so now I stand corrected.

05:25.957 --> 05:30.367
For whatever reason,
your path has led you here.

05:32.713 --> 05:34.215
And now you're one of us.

05:38.261 --> 05:39.846
Welcome, brother.

05:40.805 --> 05:45.434
Thank you... brother.

05:52.191 --> 05:53.192
Morning, Jack.

05:57.905 --> 05:59.782
Must be nice to wake up
in your own bed.

06:00.408 --> 06:03.202
Yeah. Home sweet home.

06:04.579 --> 06:07.780
Listen, I was wondering if I could
borrow your first aid kit.

06:09.458 --> 06:12.420
I've twisted my ankle.

06:16.591 --> 06:19.385
- You want me to take a look at it?
- No, you're all right.

06:20.094 --> 06:23.514
- I've taped my share of ankles.
- Right.

06:28.227 --> 06:29.395
Thanks.

06:32.315 --> 06:34.390
Something wrong, Hurley?

06:34.484 --> 06:39.228
No, just keeping Desmond company...

06:41.324 --> 06:43.065
...because we're friends.

06:45.369 --> 06:47.914
- Bring that back when you're done.
- Absolutely.

06:51.000 --> 06:54.253
What the hell was that?
Do you want him to get suspicious?

06:54.337 --> 06:55.421
Suspicious of what?

06:57.715 --> 07:00.092
This is like when
you knew Claire was drowning.

07:00.176 --> 07:03.460
That's why you got the first aid kit,
someone's gonna get hurt.

07:03.554 --> 07:06.349
- Is it me?
- No. This is just a precaution.

07:06.432 --> 07:10.301
Look, dude, you want me to take you
to the wire, I want an explanation.

07:19.695 --> 07:24.189
I saw a sequence of events.
Things that are gonna happen.

07:24.575 --> 07:30.122
- What'd you see?
- It was like a jigsaw puzzle.

07:30.206 --> 07:32.698
Only I didn't have
the picture on the box,

07:32.792 --> 07:35.086
so I don't know how
the pieces fit, exactly.

07:35.169 --> 07:36.994
One of the pieces, the first one...

07:40.925 --> 07:44.043
It was you pulling the cable
out of the sand.

07:46.722 --> 07:48.266
So what're the other pieces?

07:48.850 --> 07:52.468
If I tell you that,
it'll change the picture on the box.

07:52.562 --> 07:57.358
So what? Isn't that the point?
Preventing something bad?

07:58.151 --> 07:59.485
Not this time.

07:59.569 --> 08:02.363
So you're not trying to stop
something from happening.

08:03.865 --> 08:05.575
You actually want it to happen?

08:16.377 --> 08:18.035
More than anything.

08:28.055 --> 08:30.214
Hey, Freckles, you home?

08:31.017 --> 08:33.561
Thought you weren't
allowed to use nicknames.

08:33.644 --> 08:38.858
You weren't around
when I lost the bet, so you're...

08:41.527 --> 08:42.528
...exempt.

08:48.201 --> 08:52.205
- What's up?
- I wanted to ask you something.

08:52.288 --> 08:53.456
Yeah?

08:55.708 --> 08:57.084
I'm up here.

09:02.590 --> 09:03.789
Did you tell him?

09:04.383 --> 09:06.177
Did I tell who, what?

09:06.260 --> 09:11.724
You know, did you tell the doc
about you and me?

09:14.644 --> 09:17.928
No. But he knows.

09:18.481 --> 09:21.025
He saw us on one of their
surveillance monitors.

09:21.108 --> 09:24.529
- You said the camera was broken.
- Well, they had another camera.

09:24.987 --> 09:26.812
Those perverts.

09:27.114 --> 09:29.242
Anyway, he knows.

09:30.409 --> 09:33.079
Well, now that that's out of the way...

09:34.580 --> 09:37.124
How about a little afternoon delight?

09:40.795 --> 09:42.620
- That means sex.
- I know.

09:42.713 --> 09:43.996
Come on, Freckles, wait!

09:44.966 --> 09:48.386
- You need me to make you a mix tape?
- Yeah, why don't you do that.

09:56.394 --> 09:58.688
Dude, you're gonna
have to tell me again.

09:58.771 --> 10:02.441
- What do we need Jin for?
- Because he was there with us.

10:02.525 --> 10:05.194
On the beach, when I find the cable.

10:06.154 --> 10:07.186
This way.

10:07.280 --> 10:08.447
Here it is!

10:08.531 --> 10:11.784
- That's right.
- In one of your puzzle flashes.

10:16.914 --> 10:20.032
So if he doesn't come,

10:20.126 --> 10:23.744
then neither does the "someone"
you won't tell me anything about.

10:23.838 --> 10:25.829
That'd be the long and short of it.

10:29.051 --> 10:32.503
But I have no bloody idea how
I'm gonna get him to come with us.

10:33.347 --> 10:34.432
Watch the master.

10:41.564 --> 10:45.182
- Camping?
- Yeah, sleeping under the stars,

10:45.276 --> 10:47.351
a fire on the beach...

10:47.445 --> 10:48.946
Marshmallows.

10:50.072 --> 10:52.481
Camping.

10:58.873 --> 11:02.043
- Yes.
- Everybody likes marshmallows.

11:02.585 --> 11:06.255
Good man. Get food, water...

11:06.339 --> 11:09.133
- Where are you going?
- We need one more.

11:11.677 --> 11:14.003
How daft do you think I am?

11:14.096 --> 11:19.341
This isn't a camping trip.
You've had another vision, haven't you?

11:21.604 --> 11:22.772
What was it this time?

11:25.566 --> 11:27.308
Someone's coming to the island.

11:28.319 --> 11:31.280
"Coming?" As in someone
who's not already here?

11:31.364 --> 11:32.698
How is that gonna happen?

11:34.826 --> 11:35.858
I can't tell you.

11:38.704 --> 11:40.362
It's got nothing to do with me?

11:40.456 --> 11:43.490
Well, you're a part of it,
as are Jin and Hurley.

11:43.584 --> 11:45.169
Right, but with all due respect,

11:45.253 --> 11:48.673
you haven't previously told Jin
or Hurley that they're gonna die.

11:51.717 --> 11:54.293
Well, that's not gonna happen.
Not this time.

12:02.145 --> 12:03.604
Can I bring my guitar?

12:04.939 --> 12:06.399
Absolutely.

12:08.401 --> 12:09.652
All right, I'm in.

12:11.279 --> 12:13.020
You had me worried for a second.

12:44.020 --> 12:45.021
This is it!

12:47.899 --> 12:49.640
Well, how can you tell?

12:49.734 --> 12:52.487
That's where I followed
the wire into the jungle.

12:53.070 --> 12:54.353
Where is it then?

12:58.284 --> 12:59.483
Way to go, dude!

13:03.539 --> 13:04.874
Here it is!

13:08.002 --> 13:09.003
<i>Here it is!</i>

13:10.880 --> 13:14.050
Just one thing. Last time I followed
this wire into the jungle,

13:14.133 --> 13:17.501
I almost got kebabbed by one of
Rousseau's spiky deathtrap things.

13:21.182 --> 13:24.143
We're not going into the jungle.
Well, not yet.

13:24.227 --> 13:28.231
It's getting late.
So we'll camp here the night.

13:28.731 --> 13:30.389
Camp.

13:33.903 --> 13:35.363
So when do they get here?

13:36.614 --> 13:38.606
Your mysterious someone?

13:39.992 --> 13:40.993
Soon.

13:50.044 --> 13:53.078
You do realize you are free
to talk again, Brother Desmond.

13:56.467 --> 13:58.459
Used to being quiet, I suppose.

14:00.263 --> 14:01.211
Moriah.

14:02.932 --> 14:06.936
I find the name the brothers
have chosen for the wine made here...

14:08.437 --> 14:11.472
-...interesting.
- And why is that, brother?

14:11.566 --> 14:15.017
Well, Moriah is the mountain where
Abraham was asked to kill Isaac.

14:16.696 --> 14:20.366
It's not the exactly the most
festive locale, is it?

14:20.449 --> 14:22.743
And yet God spared Isaac.

14:23.327 --> 14:26.445
Well, one might argue that
God need not have asked

14:26.539 --> 14:29.083
Abraham to sacrifice his son
in the first place.

14:30.418 --> 14:33.754
Then it wouldn't have been
much of a test, would it, brother?

14:34.255 --> 14:37.133
Perhaps you underestimate
the value of sacrifice.

14:38.426 --> 14:42.013
Brother Desmond,
I met this man down by the gates.

14:42.096 --> 14:44.088
Says he needs to have a word with you.

14:50.480 --> 14:51.856
Sorry, sir.

15:01.032 --> 15:02.690
Forgive me, brother.

15:19.258 --> 15:21.750
- Hey.
- Hey.

15:23.262 --> 15:26.182
- The oatmeal's awesome.
- It is, huh?

15:29.519 --> 15:33.053
- It's strange, huh?
- What's that?

15:33.523 --> 15:38.945
Being back. Not looking
for a way out of a cage.

15:39.028 --> 15:43.032
Not finding a reason to go running
off into the jungle again.

15:43.115 --> 15:45.608
I almost don't know
what to do with myself.

15:46.452 --> 15:50.456
Well, enjoy it. I'm sure something
will go wrong soon enough.

15:54.669 --> 15:58.840
Well, my big,
dangerous adventure for tonight

15:58.923 --> 16:02.207
is gonna be doing the dishes...
in the ocean.

16:03.177 --> 16:05.753
- Be careful.
- I'll try.

16:08.724 --> 16:12.228
- Can I borrow that spoon?
- Yeah.

16:19.402 --> 16:20.403
Thanks.

16:29.162 --> 16:31.654
- Good night.
- Yeah, good night.

17:00.651 --> 17:02.726
What, my doorbell busted again?

17:04.947 --> 17:09.202
- What the hell are you doing?
- Shut up and don't talk.

17:18.461 --> 17:21.912
- You crying?
- I said shut up.

17:28.429 --> 17:29.597
You got it.

18:23.317 --> 18:27.321
Dude, I love the part about the bird.
There was a bird, right?

18:27.405 --> 18:30.074
- You.
- Me? OK...

18:30.825 --> 18:34.276
Have you heard the one
about the Chupacabra?

18:34.370 --> 18:35.872
Chupa...?

18:35.955 --> 18:39.792
Yeah, it's like this bear
with spines, but Mexican...

18:39.876 --> 18:40.877
Thanks.

18:43.337 --> 18:44.338
Who's that?

18:52.680 --> 18:54.140
Her name's Penny.

18:55.016 --> 18:57.935
That's not bad, Des.
Not bad at all.

18:58.019 --> 19:01.606
So how did you manage to
leave her behind and come here?

19:04.609 --> 19:06.736
Because I'm a coward.

19:07.153 --> 19:08.488
Sorry.

19:10.281 --> 19:11.939
You and me both, pal.

19:14.076 --> 19:17.278
You know, I tried to run away from her,
and she tracked me down.

19:19.373 --> 19:24.118
"With enough money and determination,
you can find anyone," she said.

19:26.047 --> 19:31.010
I used to get through my nights
thinking that she actually meant it,

19:31.093 --> 19:33.471
that she never gave up.

19:34.680 --> 19:37.256
That, maybe, she spent
the last three years...

19:38.810 --> 19:40.520
...looking for me.

19:49.612 --> 19:50.780
What's that?

20:03.543 --> 20:06.118
- Is that a helicopter?
- Rescue!

20:14.887 --> 20:17.463
Is that how a helicopter's
supposed to sound?

20:19.475 --> 20:20.674
No.

20:41.747 --> 20:42.947
We gotta go out there.

20:43.040 --> 20:44.865
- Out there?
- Well, yeah.

20:44.959 --> 20:47.503
- In what?
- Well, we gotta do something!

20:49.547 --> 20:50.548
Look!

20:51.799 --> 20:52.800
Look!

21:06.856 --> 21:08.847
Oh, my God.

21:15.364 --> 21:17.606
- Pallet?
- Nah, dude. It's not a food drop.

21:17.700 --> 21:20.411
You saw the beacon thing.
Someone, like, ejected.

21:20.495 --> 21:23.779
But that was a helicopter.
You can't eject from a helicopter.

21:23.873 --> 21:27.460
Well, maybe they jumped.
All that matters is that they're here.

21:27.543 --> 21:29.504
They?
How do we even know it's a person?

21:29.587 --> 21:31.495
Because he said "someone" was coming.

21:34.550 --> 21:38.304
- Where're you going?
- Out to where it fell. Let's go.

21:38.387 --> 21:41.641
No. Whoa, slow down.
We're not going into the jungle

21:41.724 --> 21:44.018
- in the middle of the night.
- Yes, we are.

21:44.602 --> 21:48.387
Were you even listening to Hurley when
he mentioned Rousseau's deathtrap?

21:48.481 --> 21:50.973
It's gonna be light in two hours,
we'll wait...

21:51.067 --> 21:54.101
- She can't wait!
- "She?"

21:54.195 --> 21:57.396
They! Whoever it is, could be hurt.

21:58.115 --> 21:59.940
We have to go, all four of us. Now.

22:00.409 --> 22:01.744
Why?

22:01.828 --> 22:04.539
Because that's the way
it's supposed to happen.

22:07.333 --> 22:10.336
Right, well, I guess it's
supposed to happen without me.

22:28.813 --> 22:30.804
We'll leave at first light, then.

22:33.192 --> 22:34.360
Together.

22:36.863 --> 22:38.062
Terrific.

22:46.539 --> 22:47.915
Is your sister in?

22:50.209 --> 22:53.087
Leave. Now.

22:55.089 --> 22:57.248
Let him be, Derek.

23:03.306 --> 23:04.891
Hello, Ruth.

23:09.479 --> 23:10.938
So you're a monk now, are you?

23:11.022 --> 23:14.609
Well, technically, I'm still
a novice till the Abbot says...

23:14.692 --> 23:16.027
Why are you here, Desmond?

23:18.946 --> 23:21.021
Now that my initiation's done...

23:23.034 --> 23:24.942
I felt like I owed you an explanation.

23:25.912 --> 23:31.834
Desmond, you could never begin
to explain what you did.

23:32.627 --> 23:34.702
You left one week before the wedding.

23:34.795 --> 23:37.423
Everything was planned,
bought and paid for.

23:37.507 --> 23:40.301
You just disappeared completely.

23:40.384 --> 23:42.345
I had a calling.

23:42.428 --> 23:46.015
We dated for six years
and the closest you ever came

23:46.098 --> 23:49.435
to a religious experience
was Celtic winning the Cup.

23:49.519 --> 23:53.272
Look, yes,
I was scared about the wedding.

23:53.356 --> 23:58.653
So I had a few pints
too many maybe, and I...

23:58.736 --> 24:01.854
I raised my eyes and I asked,

24:01.948 --> 24:05.284
"Am I doing the right thing?"

24:05.368 --> 24:08.246
And that's the last thing I remember.

24:08.329 --> 24:12.114
When I woke up, I was lying
on my back in the street,

24:12.208 --> 24:14.252
and I don't know how I got there.

24:14.335 --> 24:18.203
And there was this man
standing over me, Ruth.

24:18.673 --> 24:23.636
And he reached out his hand
and he said to me,

24:23.719 --> 24:25.377
"Can I help you, brother?"

24:26.097 --> 24:29.548
And the first thing I noticed was
the rope tied around his waist.

24:31.060 --> 24:37.014
I looked at him and I knew.
I knew I was supposed to go with him.

24:38.442 --> 24:43.823
I was supposed to leave
everything that mattered behind...

24:45.449 --> 24:49.944
Sacrifice all of it
for a greater calling.

24:53.958 --> 24:57.743
Well, it's a good thing
a bloody shepherd didn't help you up,

24:57.837 --> 25:00.715
or I suppose you'd be off
with the sheep, wouldn't ya?

25:03.676 --> 25:09.223
Next time you want to break up with
someone, Des, don't join a monastery.

25:10.308 --> 25:14.176
Just tell the girl
you're too bloody scared.

25:23.404 --> 25:24.906
You a doctor or a carpenter?

25:24.989 --> 25:27.825
What, your dad never taught you
to use a hammer?

25:28.618 --> 25:30.609
No, my dad taught me how to drink.

25:31.078 --> 25:32.580
Well, it's something.

25:35.374 --> 25:37.418
Hope I'm not interrupting.

25:38.252 --> 25:40.828
You two arguing over
who's your favourite Other?

25:40.922 --> 25:42.746
What do you want, Sawyer?

25:43.466 --> 25:45.374
What I wanted, Doc, was to inform you

25:45.468 --> 25:48.043
there's been developments
since you were AWOL.

25:50.139 --> 25:51.140
So tell me...

25:55.102 --> 25:56.844
How's your backhand?

25:59.649 --> 26:01.108
Where'd you get the table?

26:01.192 --> 26:05.279
Don't you recognize it? Fell out of the
purple haze after the hatch went blammo.

26:06.656 --> 26:10.785
If we don't play every 108 minutes,
the island's gonna explode.

26:12.829 --> 26:15.154
Finally. Something I can beat you at.

26:17.625 --> 26:20.628
You know, considering
I haven't played since I was 12,

26:20.711 --> 26:22.839
I wouldn't be too proud.

26:24.298 --> 26:26.008
What is that, 18 point?

26:28.469 --> 26:32.004
It's kinda strange, huh? Being back.

26:34.016 --> 26:35.560
Something funny?

26:36.352 --> 26:38.813
Kate said the same thing
in the kitchen last night.

26:40.398 --> 26:42.608
- She did, huh?
- She did.

26:45.862 --> 26:47.061
Nineteen point.

26:51.492 --> 26:53.150
So you guys ate together, huh?

26:53.619 --> 26:56.164
No, Juliet and I
had dinner together last night.

27:08.009 --> 27:12.054
- Best two out of three?
- You got it.

27:16.142 --> 27:18.634
- So what's next?
- Next?

27:18.728 --> 27:22.148
Yeah, you saw the wire, the
flashy thing falling out of the sky...

27:22.231 --> 27:24.275
Now what?
Maybe I can help you find...

27:24.358 --> 27:27.643
That's it. There is no "next."

27:27.737 --> 27:29.530
We find the beacon.

27:29.614 --> 27:32.189
- Why are you lying to me, mate?
- Look, mate...

27:32.867 --> 27:34.858
I've saved your life three times now.

27:34.952 --> 27:37.747
If that hasn't bought me your trust,
don't know what will.

27:39.540 --> 27:40.541
Let's move.

27:50.676 --> 27:54.013
Dude, seriously,
I'm gonna have a coronary.

27:54.096 --> 27:56.766
Actually, you're not.
And if you don't get a move on,

27:56.849 --> 28:00.186
- we're not gonna make it...
- Hey! Look at this!

28:03.397 --> 28:05.691
Can't be Rousseau's.
If it was Rousseau's,

28:05.775 --> 28:08.402
a massive rock would be
flying at my head right now.

28:10.446 --> 28:11.478
Don't move.

28:11.572 --> 28:13.533
- What are you doing...
- Don't move.

28:21.874 --> 28:24.877
Did that come down with
the flashing red light thingy?

28:28.464 --> 28:29.549
Walkie-talkie?

28:32.260 --> 28:34.929
No, dude, that's a satellite phone!

28:39.100 --> 28:41.894
- Crap. It's dead.
- Shocker.

28:49.193 --> 28:50.611
Oh, my God.

28:51.237 --> 28:52.572
Is that you?

28:57.577 --> 28:58.911
Then who is she?

29:00.288 --> 29:02.748
That would be Penny.

29:20.183 --> 29:22.810
- What's this?
- Your mix tape.

29:27.565 --> 29:29.525
Well, you gonna take it, or ain't ya?

29:31.694 --> 29:33.488
<i>The Best of Phil Collins</i>, huh?

29:33.571 --> 29:36.491
Don't get picky.
And if Bernard asks,

29:36.574 --> 29:39.452
- I don't know a thing about it.
- Thanks, James.

29:41.454 --> 29:43.445
So why'd you jump me last night?

29:44.874 --> 29:46.250
What?

29:46.334 --> 29:48.826
Because you saw the doc
hanging out with Juliet?

29:51.422 --> 29:53.998
- It is not like that.
- It's not?

29:56.177 --> 30:00.890
You ain't gotta use me, Freckles.
All you gotta do is ask.

30:12.360 --> 30:16.145
- You think it's her, don't you?
- Who?

30:17.448 --> 30:20.159
Your girl, Penny.

30:20.952 --> 30:24.121
You think it's actually her
who bailed out of the helicopter.

30:24.664 --> 30:26.655
Earlier I hoped it.

30:26.749 --> 30:28.709
Now I know it.

30:32.713 --> 30:33.881
Why didn't you tell us?

30:34.715 --> 30:38.584
- Would you've come if I had?
- Of course. Why wouldn't I?

30:40.429 --> 30:42.588
I didn't want to tell you because...

30:43.766 --> 30:45.810
...I didn't want anything to change.

30:46.519 --> 30:47.520
Fair enough.

30:48.437 --> 30:52.139
Look, if whatever you're seeing
leads to your girl getting us rescued,

30:52.233 --> 30:54.777
why would we want to
change anything? Right?

30:56.279 --> 30:57.280
Right.

31:05.872 --> 31:06.873
Right.

31:12.753 --> 31:15.756
Thanks for the heads-up about
bringing an umbrella, dude.

31:42.116 --> 31:44.160
Brother Desmond...

31:44.243 --> 31:45.661
What are you doing?

31:46.621 --> 31:50.750
Well, I believe I'm getting pissed
on our lovely wine.

31:52.293 --> 31:55.880
That bottle of our lovely wine
fetches over a hundred quid.

31:56.756 --> 31:59.467
We've only bottled
a 108 cases this year.

32:00.593 --> 32:03.930
It's just as well we've taken
a vow of poverty then, isn't it?

32:04.013 --> 32:06.724
We've also taken a vow of charity.

32:09.143 --> 32:10.478
Aye.

32:19.904 --> 32:23.658
Something tells me, Desmond,
that you're not cut out to be a monk.

32:24.575 --> 32:27.286
Well, you know,
I've had a tough week.

32:34.418 --> 32:38.996
I'm sorry for the wine.
I'll take the penance.

32:40.258 --> 32:42.552
I'm afraid you're
beyond penance, Desmond.

32:44.011 --> 32:45.805
Brother Desmond.

32:46.889 --> 32:48.432
Not anymore.

32:51.686 --> 32:53.677
Are you... Are you firing me?

32:53.771 --> 32:55.273
I am indeed.

32:57.400 --> 32:59.892
You can't do that. I heard the call.

32:59.986 --> 33:01.644
I'm sure you did hear the call.

33:01.737 --> 33:04.699
But the Abbey, clearly,
isn't where you're meant to end up.

33:05.116 --> 33:07.869
I have little doubt
that God has different plans

33:07.952 --> 33:10.705
than you being a monk, Desmond.
Bigger plans.

33:10.788 --> 33:12.071
Oh, I'm sure he does.

33:12.165 --> 33:16.294
He does. You've just spent
too much time running away

33:16.377 --> 33:19.213
to realize what you
may be running toward.

33:32.143 --> 33:33.227
Hey!

33:38.274 --> 33:39.901
What am I supposed to do now?

33:41.694 --> 33:43.602
Whatever comes next.

33:57.752 --> 33:58.867
Who's Penny?

33:59.629 --> 34:01.787
She's a chick Desmond used to date.

34:02.089 --> 34:04.133
Now he thinks she fell from the sky.

34:04.217 --> 34:07.470
So we're gonna go save her life,
and she's gonna get us rescued.

34:13.309 --> 34:16.103
Even if I spoke Korean,
it wouldn't make any sense.

34:16.187 --> 34:20.139
Hey, we'll move faster
if we stop talking. She might be hurt.

34:20.608 --> 34:22.600
I'm moving as fast as I can.

34:22.693 --> 34:25.655
In case you haven't noticed,
I'm not exactly the Flash.

34:26.030 --> 34:27.824
The Flash is pathetic.

34:28.533 --> 34:31.077
You got something against
the fastest man alive?

34:31.911 --> 34:32.995
You're insane, mate.

34:33.079 --> 34:36.780
Superman can fly around the
entire planet in the blink of an eye.

34:36.874 --> 34:39.199
Dude, if we're going by
a pure foot race,

34:39.293 --> 34:41.201
Supes would get dusted by the Flash.

34:41.295 --> 34:44.715
Why would the Man of Steel
agree to a sodding foot race?

34:44.799 --> 34:46.300
For charity?

34:46.384 --> 34:50.085
Flash would totally win, because
he can vibrate through walls and stuff.

34:50.179 --> 34:53.683
Vibration! And what would Superman do
if he came up against a wall?

34:53.766 --> 34:55.560
Well, no smashing allowed.

34:57.854 --> 35:00.148
No flying, no smashing.

35:00.231 --> 35:02.556
Any other restrictions
I need to know about?

35:04.318 --> 35:08.270
Perhaps we should fit Superman with
a pair of kryptonite ballet slippers.

35:11.075 --> 35:12.076
What the hell?

35:13.786 --> 35:14.787
Charlie, duck!

35:27.508 --> 35:28.593
Dude...

35:40.104 --> 35:41.105
This way.

35:42.773 --> 35:45.015
No, the beacon fell
this side of the rise.

35:45.109 --> 35:46.277
No, there!

35:47.195 --> 35:50.031
How about we split up?
Me and Charlie will go that way.

35:50.114 --> 35:53.399
You and Jin go around, and we'll
meet up at that ridge over there.

35:53.493 --> 35:56.496
You and Jin. I'll stick with Desmond.

36:07.882 --> 36:08.998
You said "duck."

36:10.009 --> 36:12.418
- Sorry?
- You shouted "duck."

36:14.388 --> 36:18.518
You knew, even before we set off.
You knew all this time, didn't you?

36:18.601 --> 36:20.843
- Aye.
- Why didn't you say anything?

36:20.937 --> 36:23.429
If I'd told you the truth,
you wouldn't have come.

36:23.523 --> 36:27.057
And you needed me to come...
because I was part of your vision.

36:27.151 --> 36:32.146
You thought the way you could get your
girl was if I took an arrow in the head.

36:32.240 --> 36:35.441
- You were gonna sacrifice me!
- If the flashes don't happen

36:35.535 --> 36:38.454
exactly how I saw them,
the picture changes.

36:40.540 --> 36:42.698
I was supposed to let you die, Charlie.

36:42.792 --> 36:46.462
- What's that supposed to mean?
- It means it's bloody pointless!

36:47.713 --> 36:50.508
I keep saving your life.
And what good has it done?

36:50.633 --> 36:55.044
It's going to keep happening. Maybe
that's the point? Maybe it's a test.

36:55.138 --> 36:57.932
- A test?
- Like God testing Abraham!

36:58.015 --> 37:02.145
Except I failed.
Because I changed what I saw.

37:17.910 --> 37:20.830
Hey! Hey, can you hear me?

37:20.913 --> 37:22.571
Hello!

37:27.295 --> 37:28.754
Dude, she's not moving.

37:32.091 --> 37:36.012
I'm sorry, Penny. I'm sorry.

37:50.693 --> 37:53.237
I was afraid you'd left
without saying goodbye.

37:53.321 --> 37:54.697
No.

37:57.200 --> 37:59.275
I nearly took this with me.

38:03.664 --> 38:04.947
If you're not in a hurry,

38:05.041 --> 38:08.826
Brother Martin's heading into town
in a few hours. He can give you a ride.

38:09.879 --> 38:12.965
That is, if you don't mind
doing some heavy lifting.

38:15.384 --> 38:17.543
All ten cases are ready to go.

38:17.887 --> 38:20.515
Desmond, there,
is just getting the last one.

38:20.598 --> 38:23.226
Thank you, and my father
sent the check in advance.

38:23.309 --> 38:25.770
Please thank him for his
generous donation.

38:25.853 --> 38:27.761
Always a pleasure to see you.

38:31.275 --> 38:32.527
Goodbye, Desmond.

38:39.867 --> 38:42.328
I think we should be able
to fit it all in the back,

38:42.411 --> 38:44.486
and if not, we'll
put the rest in the front.

38:46.999 --> 38:48.084
Is that all right?

38:50.545 --> 38:51.712
Absolutely.

39:04.100 --> 39:05.841
You'd better drive safe, Miss.

39:06.602 --> 39:10.054
This vineyard only makes a limited
number of these cases each year.

39:10.148 --> 39:13.818
- Is that so?
- It's because the monks are lazy.

39:14.986 --> 39:17.561
It's easier making
grape jelly than wine.

39:18.239 --> 39:20.231
And how do you know
so much about monks?

39:20.324 --> 39:22.733
- Because I'm an ex-monk.
- Really?

39:22.827 --> 39:26.278
As of last night. I was fired.

39:28.833 --> 39:30.543
Oh, it wasn't that funny.

39:30.626 --> 39:34.213
I'm sorry, I've never...
I didn't know monks could be fired.

39:34.297 --> 39:35.412
Well, they can.

39:36.174 --> 39:38.885
I was told in no uncertain terms that

39:38.968 --> 39:41.596
the Abbey wasn't where
I was meant to end up.

39:41.679 --> 39:45.381
It's just a step along a path.

39:45.475 --> 39:48.227
God allegedly has bigger plans for me.

39:53.524 --> 39:56.527
Something tells me
you don't entirely believe that.

39:56.611 --> 39:59.572
- I suspect that's because I don't.
- Maybe they're right.

39:59.655 --> 40:02.773
If you hadn't got fired,
we wouldn't have met, and then...

40:02.867 --> 40:06.235
How could you possibly help me
unload these crates in Carlisle.

40:07.830 --> 40:10.041
Did I say I was coming
to Carlisle with you?

40:10.833 --> 40:12.032
Not yet.

40:22.970 --> 40:25.723
Of course, if an ex-monk
already has plans, then...

40:25.807 --> 40:28.132
I don't usually get into cars
with strangers.

40:28.226 --> 40:30.634
Well, in that case, I'm Penelope.

40:32.939 --> 40:33.971
Penny.

40:35.775 --> 40:37.276
Desmond.

40:39.779 --> 40:41.322
Very nice to meet you, Penny.

40:51.916 --> 40:52.948
She's alive!

40:55.294 --> 40:58.495
Stand back! Get away from her!

41:00.758 --> 41:03.000
I'm here. I'm here, Penny.

41:03.094 --> 41:05.721
- Be careful...
- Just get off, Charlie.

41:05.805 --> 41:07.796
Sorry, Penny, sorry...

41:15.481 --> 41:16.764
Desmond...
